  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 111 PM MDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nFriday...we warm up once again and expect temps around 90F over the \nplains with mid 80s valleys. Only isolated storms are expected in \nthe afternoon/early evening. We will see a bit more of a fire \nweather risks today as it will be breezy and dry, and Elevated fire \nweather conditions will once again be possible over the San Luis \nValley, the lower elevations of Fremont and Chaffee counties and \nwestern Pueblo county. \n\nSaturday...a fairly stout cool front move down the plains Saturday \nmorning. However showers and thunderstorms are still expected to by \nmainly isolated over the region. It will be cooler with highs in the \n80s across the valleys and plains.\n\nSunday...Temperatures are forecast to shoot up again, with values in \nthe mid to upper 90s across the plains and mid 80s valleys. showers \nwill be isolated across the plains.\n\nAnother cold front moves across the region late Sunday into early \nMonday and and max temps at the beginning of the week fall back down \nin the 80s Monday, with even cooler weather moving into for Tuesday. \nWe should see a better chance of showers and storms on these two \ndays as we will see the monsoon plume get reinvigorated over the \nregion and a disturbance comes across the region.\n\nIt appears an unsettled pattern will remain across the region \nthrough the rest of the week bringing in some cooler weather and \nbetter chances of precip. \\/Hodanish",
